    "description": "Bolder Industries converts end-of-life tires into recovered carbon black, petrochemical products, steel, and related outputs for industrial customers. Its end markets include tire manufacturing, rubber and plastics production, and other users seeking lower-carbon feedstocks and circular-economy inputs. The operating model is asset-heavy because performance depends on proprietary processing facilities, feedstock supply, and long-term offtake relationships rather than an asset-light services platform. Public materials point to operating activity in Missouri and expansion activity in Indiana, with additional international development activity disclosed by the company. CIM Group expanded its investment in 2021, Tiger Infrastructure announced a major growth investment in 2025, and the current ownership structure has not been publicly disclosed.",
